# Multi-Tenant Business Scope — REQUIRED for every tenant CRUD

Every Spring Boot service / repository / controller under `backend/bizly-api/*`
that touches a **tenant-owned** table (one with a `business_id` column) MUST
filter and stamp by tenant. The current tenant lives in
`com.<module>.security.BusinessContextHolder`, populated by `InternalAuthFilter`
from the `X-Business-Id` / `X-Role-Level` / `X-Business-Override` headers.

## Tenant table cheat sheet

`PM_PRODUCT`, `PM_PRODUCT_ITEMS`, `PM_CUSTOMER_SALE`, `PM_CUSTOMER_SALE_LINE`,
`BM_SERVICE_ITEM`, `BM_APPOINTMENT`, `KYC_CUSTOMER`, `KYC_CUSTOMER_ORDER`,
`SETTINGS_DASHBOARD`, `SETTINGS_WIDGET`, `SETTINGS_REPORT`, `SETTINGS_QUERY_DEF`,
`SETTINGS_DASH_*_GRANT`, `SETTINGS_REPORT_*_GRANT`, `SETTINGS_QDEF_*_GRANT`,
`NOTIF_INBOX`, `NOTIF_BROADCAST_MESSAGE`, `NOTIF_EMAIL_TEMPLATE`,
`UM_USER`, `UM_AUDIT_LOG`.

Catalogs that stay **global** (never scope, never stamp): `UM_ROLE`,
`UM_ROLE_LEVEL`, `UM_USER_ROLE`, `UM_MENUS`, `UM_APPLICATIONS`, `UM_BUSINESS`.

## Repository contract

Expose tenant-scoped finders **before** anyone can write a service against the
repository:

```java
// BAD — public JpaRepository surface lets callers read ANY tenant's data
public interface ProductRepository extends JpaRepository<Product, Long> {}

// GOOD — every business-aware finder takes a businessId param
public interface ProductRepository extends JpaRepository<Product, Long> {
  Optional<Product> findByIdAndBusinessId(Long id, Long businessId);
  Page<Product> findAllByBusinessId(Long businessId, Pageable pageable);
}
```

For Settings tables where built-in / admin templates live as
`business_id IS NULL`, use the `*ForBusinessOrGlobal` pattern:

```java
@Query("SELECT r FROM SettingsReport r WHERE r.id = :id "
     + "AND (r.businessId IS NULL OR r.businessId = :businessId)")
Optional<SettingsReport> findByIdForBusinessOrGlobal(@Param("id") Long id,
    @Param("businessId") Long businessId);
```

## Service contract

```java
@Override
public AddXResponse add(AddXRequest req) {
  Long businessId = BusinessContextHolder.requireBusinessId();
  X x = new X();
  x.setBusinessId(businessId);   // ← stamp on create
  // …
  repository.save(x);
  return new AddXResponse(x.getId());
}

@Override
public GetXResponse get(GetXRequest req) {
  Long businessId = BusinessContextHolder.requireBusinessId();
  X x = repository.findByIdAndBusinessId(req.getId(), businessId)   // ← scoped read
    .orElseThrow(() -> new ServiceException(ApiMessages.X_NOT_FOUND, HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND));
  return mapToResponse(x);
}
```

**Update / delete** MUST load via `findByIdAndBusinessId` so a cross-tenant id
is treated as 404 — never `repository.findById(id)` and then mutate.

## SUPER_ADMIN bypass

Admin screens that legitimately need to read across tenants check
`BusinessContextHolder.canBypassTenant()` (true when role-level=ADMIN) and may
fall back to un-scoped finders:

```java
if (BusinessContextHolder.canBypassTenant()) {
  return repository.findAll(pageable);             // cross-tenant
}
Long businessId = BusinessContextHolder.requireBusinessId();
return repository.findAllByBusinessId(businessId, pageable);   // tenant only
```

The `X-Business-Override` header is already substituted into
`currentBusinessId()` automatically, so the same code transparently honours the
SUPER_ADMIN global context switcher.

## Audit + notifications

`UM.AuditAspect` and `BM.NotifInboxServiceImpl#publish` stamp `business_id`
from `BusinessContextHolder.currentBusinessId()` (which may be `NULL` for
system-level events).

## Definition of done — checklist

- [ ] Entity has a `@Column(name = "business_id") private Long businessId` field
      with getter/setter.
- [ ] Repository exposes `findByIdAndBusinessId` and `findAllByBusinessId`
      (or `*ForBusinessOrGlobal` for tables with global templates).
- [ ] Service `add` calls `BusinessContextHolder.requireBusinessId()` and
      stamps the new entity (or `currentBusinessId()` if global rows are valid).
- [ ] Service `update` / `delete` load via the scoped finder, never raw
      `findById` / `existsById` / `deleteById`.
- [ ] Service `get` / `gets` use the scoped finder, with an admin-bypass
      branch where appropriate.
- [ ] DDL: the table has a `BUSINESS_ID NUMBER` column, an index on it, and an
      FK to `UM.UM_BUSINESS(ID)`. The comprehensive patch
      `um/src/main/resources/db/oracle/patch-business-scope-all-tenant-tables-oracle.sql`
      already covers every table in the cheat sheet; **add a new table to
      that script and re-run** rather than writing a new ad-hoc patch.
- [ ] Frontend never sends `business_id` in request bodies — the value comes
      from the JWT on the gateway. Reject it if the DTO accidentally exposes it.

